# Files whose exact bytes matter: keep LF even on Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true would
# otherwise turn them into CRLF).
# - Shell scripts run inside Linux containers and CI; /bin/sh rejects CRLF.
# - SQL migrations are embedded by sqlx with a checksum of their bytes: a CRLF build would refuse
#   a database migrated by an LF build ("migration N was previously applied but has been modified").
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
